{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-342496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}, & x\\in [-3,0] \\\\ -{x}^{2}, & x\\in (0,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. Find the value to which the Fourier series of the $6$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is converging when $x=2.$\n\nThe Fourier series converges to {{field-1}} when $x=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-342496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a $2L$-periodic piecewise smooth function with the corresponding Fourier series\n\n$$\nS(x)=\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x).\n$$\n\nThen, the series converges for all $x\\in R.$\n\n- If $f(x)$ is continuous at $x,$ then the series converges to the value of the function at this point:\n\n$$\nS(x)=f(x)\n$$\n\n- If $f(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x,$ then the series converges to the midpoint between the values of left- and right-sided limits of the function at this point:\n\n$$\nS(x)=\\frac{{f}^{-}(x)+{f}^{+}(x)}{2}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{-}(x)$ and ${f}^{-}(x)$ are the left- and right-sided limits of the function at this point, respectively.\n\nNotice that the $6$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of our function $F(x)$ is continuous at $x=2.$ \n\nTherefore, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ converges to \n\n$$\nf(2)=-{2}^{2}=-4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-342496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7c7235a4b7f5a4c12e714ca2bb563d218691d40ad9766045940d8824b3afaf8"} {"question" "q-342496" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-342496" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-342573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the function $F(x)=|x|$ defined on $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ The Fourier series of the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{\\pi }{2}-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{\\pi (2n-1)^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡((2n-1)x).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.At $x=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡((2n-1)\\cdot 0)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is \n{{field-2}}\nat $x=0,$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(0)={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}={{field-4}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-342573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite our Fourier series as\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{4}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡((2n-1)x).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that at $x=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡((2n-1)\\cdot 0)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=1.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is $\\text{continuous}$ at $x=0,$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(0)=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{4}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡((2n-1)\\cdot 0) \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{4}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}\\cdot 1 \\\\ -\\frac{\\pi }{2} & =-\\frac{4}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}} \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}} & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-342573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7c7235a4b7f5a4c12e714ca2bb563d218691d40ad9766045940d8824b3afaf8"} {"question" "q-342573" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-342573" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-1)^{n+1}"] ["math" "(-1)^{n}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-342573" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-342573" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-342573" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "continuous"] ["text" "discontinuous"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-342573" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "continuous"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-342573" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-342573" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "0.5"] ["math" "1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-342573" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-342573" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-342573" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-342573" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-343364" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+2}, & x\\in [-2,0) \\\\ 1, & x\\in [0,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. Find the value to which the Fourier series of the $4$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ converges when $x=-2.$\n\nThe Fourier series converges to {{field-1}} when $x=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-343364" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a $2L$-periodic piecewise smooth function with the corresponding Fourier series\n\n$$\nS(x)=\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x).\n$$\n\nThen, the series converges for all $x\\in R.$\n\n- If $f(x)$ is continuous at $x,$ then the series converges to the value of the function at this point:\n\n$$\nS(x)=f(x)\n$$\n\n- If $f(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x,$ then the series converges to the midpoint between the values of left- and right-sided limits of the function at this point:\n\n$$\nS(x)=\\frac{{f}^{-}(x)+{f}^{+}(x)}{2}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{-}(x)$ and ${f}^{+}(x)$ are the left- and right-sided limits of the function at this point, respectively.\n\nNotice that the $4$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of our function $F(x)$ is not continuous at $x=-2.$ The one-sided limits at this point are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-}(-2) & ={lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{-}}f(x)=1 \\\\ {f}^{+}(-2) & ={lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}f(x)={e}^{-2+2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ converges to \n\n$$\n\\frac{{f}^{-}(-2)+{f}^{+}(-2)}{2}=\\frac{1+1}{2}=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-343364" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7c7235a4b7f5a4c12e714ca2bb563d218691d40ad9766045940d8824b3afaf8"} {"question" "q-343364" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-343364" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-343438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}-1, & x\\in [-4,0] \\\\ 3, & x\\in (0,4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. The Fourier series of the $8$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼1+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{\\pi (2n-1)}sin\\,(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi x}{4}).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.At $x=-2,$ we have\n\n$$\nsin\\,(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi \\cdot (-2)}{4})={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is \n{{field-2}}\nat $x=-2,$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(-2)={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1}={{field-4}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-343438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite our Fourier series as\n\n$$\nf(x)∼1+\\frac{8}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot sin\\,(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi x}{4}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that at $x=-2,$ we have\n\n$$\nsin\\,(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi \\cdot (-2)}{4})=sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-n\\pi )=(-1)^{n}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is $\\text{continuous}$ at $x=-2,$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(-2)=-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2) & =1+\\frac{8}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot sin\\,(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi \\cdot (-2)}{4}) \\\\ -1 & =1+\\frac{8}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot (-1)^{n} \\\\ -2 & =\\frac{8}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{2n-1} \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{2n-1} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-343438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7c7235a4b7f5a4c12e714ca2bb563d218691d40ad9766045940d8824b3afaf8"} {"question" "q-343438" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073830/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6af7f2b4c93754be1006c1ddfd7f72aa981f1dc7d370a0d2a7241e65e645341"} {"question" "q-343438" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-1)^{n+1}"] ["math" "(-1)^{n}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/ho